WEBVTT

00:07.090 --> 00:09.752
Thanks, Mom.
This is a perfect first job for him.

00:09.926 --> 00:10.950
First job?

00:11.127 --> 00:13.687
I think you're looking at
the birth of a career.

00:18.168 --> 00:21.626
I was gonna have him put up fliers,
but I didn't trust him with a staple gun.

00:22.072 --> 00:25.872
- How much are you paying him?
- Obviously too much, look at him.

00:29.646 --> 00:33.514
&lt;i>For the record, I promised him $20
and a Playboy magazine.&lt;/i>

00:33.683 --> 00:34.741
&lt;i>Playboy?&lt;/i>

00:34.918 --> 00:39.480
Don't worry. I'll Magic Marker
over the ta-tas and hoo-hoos.

00:39.923 --> 00:42.892
Oh, that's disturbing on so many levels.

00:52.202 --> 00:53.533
I should have hired a monkey.

00:54.704 --> 00:57.605
You mean a different monkey.

01:07.283 --> 01:09.581
So Little Jughead's earning a paycheck?

01:09.753 --> 01:13.314
Well, it's not really a paycheck,
and he's not really earning it.

01:13.490 --> 01:14.957
And we don't call him-

01:15.125 --> 01:17.252
I guess I gotta give you Jughead.

01:17.694 --> 01:19.161
I remember my first job.

01:19.329 --> 01:20.455
Slaughterhouse.

01:20.630 --> 01:23.258
Stripping out sheep intestines
for the condom companies.

01:27.937 --> 01:30.428
Not as sexy as it sounds.

01:30.874 --> 01:32.341
I was a fluffer in a pet salon.

01:34.711 --> 01:36.144
You know, with a blow-dryer.

01:36.312 --> 01:38.473
Huh. I was going
a completely different way.

01:42.118 --> 01:43.142
What are you doing?

01:43.319 --> 01:47.016
Thanks to Grandma, I'm reading
an interview with Jimmy Kimmel.

01:48.191 --> 01:51.058
- Hey, Alan, you got any cash?
- Yeah, why?

01:51.227 --> 01:53.354
- I need to borrow some.
- What for?

01:53.530 --> 01:55.225
What are you, my mother?

01:55.398 --> 01:57.798
Just give me a few bucks,
save me a trip to the ATM.

01:57.967 --> 02:00.765
- When will I get it back?
- I don't know. Tomorrow?

02:00.937 --> 02:03.064
Okay. How much do you need?

02:03.239 --> 02:04.467
Just a couple hundred.

02:06.142 --> 02:09.202
A couple hundred?
Who carries around that kind of money?

02:09.379 --> 02:12.348
Well, let's see.
Strippers, bookies, prostitutes...

02:12.515 --> 02:15.609
...and not entirely coincidentally, me.

02:16.252 --> 02:20.689
Well, I've only got, uh, 35-
Uh, $38.

02:20.857 --> 02:24.349
That's it?
That's your walking-around money?

02:24.527 --> 02:26.586
It's the perfect amount
in case I get mugged.

02:26.763 --> 02:29.891
Not so little that my attacker
would get angry and pistol-whip me...

02:30.066 --> 02:32.125
...yet not so much
that I would fight for it...

02:32.302 --> 02:34.964
...and possibly get shot
while wrestling for the gun.

02:38.107 --> 02:41.133
- So you got $38?
- Yup.

02:41.311 --> 02:42.778
Just out of curiosity...

02:42.946 --> 02:45.574
...how much money would it take
to wrestle a gun from a mugger?

02:45.748 --> 02:48.683
Assuming a small- to medium-sized mugger,
at least 40.

02:50.820 --> 02:52.185
Fine. So give me the 38.

02:52.355 --> 02:53.754
- All of it?
- Why not?

02:53.923 --> 02:57.689
- Then I've got nothing.
- And you think $38 changes that?

02:58.728 --> 03:00.787
What if I decide to go out
and have some fun?

03:00.964 --> 03:03.262
Thirty-eight dollars worth of fun?

03:04.033 --> 03:06.092
I wouldn't spend all of it.

03:07.136 --> 03:09.468
Okay. Okay, look.
You're not going out to have fun.

03:09.639 --> 03:12.506
You never go out to have fun. Because
you know why? You're not a fun guy.

03:13.843 --> 03:17.176
Oh, I am very much a fun guy. We just
have very different definitions of "fun"...

03:17.347 --> 03:21.044
...and mine doesn't include
urinary-tract infections and dry heaving.

03:22.685 --> 03:25.245
Just give me the money, you big fruit.

03:25.755 --> 03:27.916
Thirty-eight dollars...

03:28.925 --> 03:32.053
If it had been 40,
we'd be wrestling, my friend.

03:37.200 --> 03:39.134
ALAN: Hey, Charlie.

03:46.609 --> 03:48.236
You got my money?

03:51.514 --> 03:52.981
Charlie.

03:53.149 --> 03:54.582
I'm trying to sleep, Alan.

03:54.751 --> 03:57.276
I've gotta go to work
and you said you'd have my money.

03:57.453 --> 04:00.115
- Oh, for God's sake.
- You don't even have to get up...

04:00.290 --> 04:01.587
...just tell me where it is.

04:01.758 --> 04:03.623
Well, the last I saw any of it...

04:03.793 --> 04:06.990
...it was sandwiched between two
of the loveliest man-made breasts...

04:07.163 --> 04:09.256
...that ever smacked me in the eye.

04:09.432 --> 04:13.300
Oh, Charlie, you say the sweetest things.

04:13.870 --> 04:16.566
Oh, Ginger, this is my brother, Alan.
Alan, Ginger.

04:17.006 --> 04:18.439
Hi.

04:18.608 --> 04:21.304
Hi. So bottom line,
you don't have my money?

04:21.744 --> 04:23.143
- No.
- The money you promised...

04:23.313 --> 04:24.439
...to pay back today?

04:24.614 --> 04:27.242
- Today hasn't even started yet.
- It started for me.

04:27.417 --> 04:29.942
That's only because
you're on douchebag savings time.

04:31.187 --> 04:32.654
Can we please talk about this...

04:32.822 --> 04:36.986
...when one of us doesn't have a warm,
firm buttock nestled against his groin?

04:37.427 --> 04:38.951
Oh, dear Lord.

04:39.128 --> 04:40.595
So you'll get it by tonight?

04:40.763 --> 04:43.527
I'm hoping to get it
as soon as you close the door.

04:47.170 --> 04:48.660
You really out of cash?

04:48.838 --> 04:51.898
Don't worry, I got hooker money.

05:01.351 --> 05:04.514
&lt;i>When you're hungry at school
You need to know&lt;/i>

05:04.687 --> 05:06.052
&lt;i>Paste, yes&lt;/i>

05:06.222 --> 05:07.712
&lt;i>Boogers, no&lt;/i>

05:13.162 --> 05:15.995
- Hey.
- How was your day, darling?

05:16.499 --> 05:20.458
Fine. Except I had to pay for lunch
with my lucky Sacagawea dollar.

05:21.004 --> 05:22.995
What kind of lunch
can you get for a dollar?

05:23.172 --> 05:24.434
Two gas station hot dogs...

05:24.607 --> 05:27.633
...that were a year old if they were a day,
thank you very much.

05:28.111 --> 05:31.569
Is Sacagawea the same Indian chick
that's on the Land O' Lakes butter?

05:32.882 --> 05:34.509
I don't know.

05:34.684 --> 05:36.345
I hope so.

05:37.720 --> 05:38.914
I'd like to believe it is.

05:40.356 --> 05:43.120
Okay, Charlie. I'm leaving.

05:43.292 --> 05:45.260
Hang on. Let me pay you.

05:49.432 --> 05:50.456
There you go.

05:50.633 --> 05:52.863
You forget I paid
for that pizza the other night?

05:53.036 --> 05:55.402
Oh, right. How much was that?

05:55.571 --> 06:00.440
Well, you got the garlic balls too,
so say, 75 bucks.

06:02.278 --> 06:04.212
- You got change for a hundred?
- Nope.

06:04.380 --> 06:07.543
- Okay, you'll pay me back.
- Count on it.

06:11.354 --> 06:14.721
Wait, wait, wait. As long as you're
doling it out, you got my 40 bucks?

06:14.891 --> 06:17.451
- Oh, sure. You got change for a hundred?
- Nope.

06:17.627 --> 06:20.619
- Okay, I'll catch you later.
- Wait.

06:21.230 --> 06:23.255
How come Berta can pay you back
and I can't?

06:23.433 --> 06:26.197
Oh, grow up.
She's not gonna pay me back.

06:26.803 --> 06:28.065
Okay, then what about me?

06:28.504 --> 06:30.699
- What about you?
- I want my $40.

06:31.240 --> 06:32.935
I only borrowed 38.

06:33.109 --> 06:35.771
Yeah, well, I find round numbers
easier to remember.

06:35.945 --> 06:39.437
- You like round numbers, do you?
- Yeah, I like round numbers.

06:39.615 --> 06:41.515
Okay, here's a round number for you.

06:41.684 --> 06:43.379
Zero.

06:44.087 --> 06:46.021
Nice, tight circular shape.

06:46.189 --> 06:48.749
Nothing gets in, nothing gets out.
Sound familiar, Alan?

06:50.259 --> 06:51.658
Are you calling me anal?

06:51.828 --> 06:54.888
That's right. A-I-A-N. "Anal."

06:56.332 --> 06:58.926
Okay, okay, okay. So bottom line...

06:59.102 --> 07:01.468
...you're not gonna pay me back.
Is that correct?

07:01.637 --> 07:04.162
Well, truth be told,
I was gonna pay you back...

07:04.340 --> 07:06.433
...but your attitude irks me.

07:06.609 --> 07:08.907
- I irk you?
- That's right.

07:09.078 --> 07:10.102
I find you irksome.

07:11.747 --> 07:14.409
You're a big, fat irk.

07:14.851 --> 07:18.480
Hey, hey. You borrow 38 dollars,
you owe me 38 dollars.

07:18.654 --> 07:21.885
Yeah, well, you've been living
in my Malibu beach house for six years.

07:22.058 --> 07:24.492
You owe me 1 million dollars.

07:25.228 --> 07:26.354
A million dollars?

07:26.863 --> 07:30.026
That's a one followed by
six tight little sphincters.

07:42.945 --> 07:43.934
Wow.

07:44.113 --> 07:47.480
- You look tired.
- Yesterday, I had a quarter tank of gas.

07:47.650 --> 07:51.848
Today, I drive a mile into Topanga Canyon,
and bang, empty.

07:52.021 --> 07:53.010
Huh.

07:53.422 --> 07:55.083
There's no cell coverage up there.

07:55.258 --> 07:57.658
So I had to hump back to the beach
to call Triple A.

07:57.827 --> 07:59.454
- Oh, that's a shame.
- Shame, my ass.

07:59.629 --> 08:02.462
How the hell did a quarter tank of gas
disappear overnight?

08:02.632 --> 08:04.122
It's a mystery.

08:08.371 --> 08:09.395
Wait a minute.

08:10.039 --> 08:11.870
I smell gasoline.

08:12.575 --> 08:13.906
Really?

08:14.310 --> 08:15.538
I don't smell anything.

08:27.456 --> 08:30.391
You have gas on your breath.
You siphoned my tank.

08:30.560 --> 08:32.551
Ah, oh, please.

08:32.728 --> 08:35.162
You think I stuck a rubber hose
down your gas tank...

08:35.331 --> 08:38.391
...sucked on it until the gas ran out
of your tank and into mine...

08:38.568 --> 08:40.866
...thereby compensating me
for the $38 you owe me?

08:43.806 --> 08:45.535
That's preposterous.

08:46.342 --> 08:49.573
Yeah. Yeah, you're right.

08:49.745 --> 08:51.804
What was I thinking?

08:59.956 --> 09:01.184
What are you doing?

09:01.691 --> 09:04.023
Do me a favor. Say...

09:04.860 --> 09:06.851
..."preposterous" again.

09:07.496 --> 09:09.896
Hey, you're crazy.

09:10.499 --> 09:12.057
Get that away from me!

09:12.235 --> 09:15.136
Oh, come on. Come on.

09:15.571 --> 09:18.699
Just for grins, say,
"Help me. My head's on fire."

09:19.242 --> 09:23.474
All right, all right. I sucked the gas
out of your car. Now, turn that off.

09:26.515 --> 09:29.484
Okay, fine. Well played.
You got your money back.

09:30.086 --> 09:31.075
Uh.

09:31.254 --> 09:35.247
Actually, uh, at 473.9 cents a gallon...

09:36.025 --> 09:39.222
...you had only $13 and 22 cents worth
in your tank.

09:39.395 --> 09:41.625
So you still owe me 24.78.

09:48.838 --> 09:50.772
- Get out.
- What?

09:50.940 --> 09:53.101
Get out of my house.

09:53.276 --> 09:54.641
You know what? I just might.

09:54.810 --> 09:57.176
No, no, no.
"Might" implies you have a choice.

09:57.346 --> 10:00.645
Oh, so you're gonna throw me out
over 24 dollars and 78 cents?

10:00.816 --> 10:04.308
No, I'm throwing you out because
you're a cheap, gas-sucking, flammable irk.

10:06.055 --> 10:07.784
I am not cheap.

10:08.224 --> 10:09.885
Leaving.

10:15.965 --> 10:18.229
Ow, ow! Hot, hot.

10:21.437 --> 10:23.871
It's no one's fault, Jake.
These things just happen.

10:24.040 --> 10:26.975
I don't know,
they seem to happen to you a lot.

10:29.211 --> 10:31.270
Oh. Hey, guys.
What are you doing here?

10:31.447 --> 10:33.278
Dad pissed off Uncle Charlie again.

10:35.184 --> 10:37.744
Uh, sorry to show up
unannounced like this.

10:37.920 --> 10:39.911
Oh, no problem.
It's always good to see you.

10:40.089 --> 10:41.852
JUDITH:
He got kicked out again?

10:43.192 --> 10:46.286
- Damn it, Alan. What did you do now?
- Oh, I didn't do anything.

10:46.462 --> 10:48.930
But I'm not gonna be staying
at Charlie's anymore...

10:49.098 --> 10:51.658
...so I thought I should bring
Jake's stuff back here...

10:51.834 --> 10:54.268
- ...until I find a place of my own.
- Fine. Good luck.

10:54.437 --> 10:58.430
Uh, but it's nobody's fault.
I just think it's time for me to move on.

10:58.607 --> 11:00.268
Okay. Good night.

11:00.443 --> 11:04.209
But FYI, Charlie's a thief, a liar,
and I suspect something of a firebug.

11:04.380 --> 11:07.577
Really? Hmm.
He always struck me as a straight-shooter.

11:07.750 --> 11:11.914
A little loosey-goosey with the liquor
and the ladies, but all in all a good fella.

11:13.622 --> 11:16.147
In what universe
is Charlie Harper a good fella?

11:17.126 --> 11:20.186
Well, I certainly don't know him
as well as you do...

11:20.363 --> 11:22.456
...so I'll just shut my pie hole.

11:23.532 --> 11:26.797
Uh, anyway, uh,
here's the rest of Jake's stuff.

11:26.969 --> 11:29.995
Uh, I'll get you my new address
as soon as I have one.

11:30.439 --> 11:31.463
- You do that.
- Okay.

11:31.640 --> 11:34.541
- So where are you gonna stay till then?
- Pie hole, Herb.

11:35.311 --> 11:36.300
Oh, I don't know.

11:36.479 --> 11:38.071
Uh, things are a
little tight right now...

11:38.247 --> 11:40.545
...so a hotel isn't really an
option, you know.

11:40.716 --> 11:43.310
Maybe the- The Y for a couple of
days, you know?

11:43.486 --> 11:44.953
Uh, but we'll see.

11:45.121 --> 11:47.316
I could, uh, sleep in my office.

11:47.490 --> 11:48.479
Uh...

11:48.657 --> 11:49.715
Or in the car.

11:49.892 --> 11:53.157
- Oh, you can't do that.
- Pie hole, pie hole, pie hole.

11:53.329 --> 11:55.991
Come on, Judith, you can't expect the man
to sleep in his car.

11:56.165 --> 11:58.497
You're good people.
Just let me get a few things.

11:59.835 --> 12:03.066
It'll be fine. He's not the kind of guy
who will overstay his welcome.

12:03.239 --> 12:05.935
He's been at his brother's for six years.

12:06.108 --> 12:09.509
Uh, Herb, would you mind giving me a hand
with the Nordic Track? It's...

12:09.678 --> 12:11.612
Oh, sure.

12:14.250 --> 12:15.945
Love you.

12:22.258 --> 12:24.226
- Hey, Charlie.
- Oh, hey, Herb. What's up?

12:24.393 --> 12:26.258
I came to pick up some stuff for Alan.

12:26.429 --> 12:28.761
- For Alan?
- Yeah, he's staying with Judith and I...

12:28.931 --> 12:30.660
...till he gets back on his feet.

12:30.833 --> 12:32.733
Gee, Herb,
I hate to be the bearer of bad news...

12:34.069 --> 12:37.436
...but I've been waiting six years for that
khaki-wearing weasel to get on his feet.

12:37.606 --> 12:38.903
Yeah, Judith mentioned that.

12:39.074 --> 12:41.508
Using a lot of the same words,
interestingly enough.

12:41.677 --> 12:45.374
He wanted to avoid having a scene,
so he asked if I'd pick up some of his stuff.

12:45.548 --> 12:48.881
- And you agreed?
- I had to get out of there, Charlie.

12:49.819 --> 12:51.343
Okay, okay, fine. What do you need?

12:51.520 --> 12:54.080
Oh, quite a few things, actually.
He gave me a list.

12:54.256 --> 12:58.283
Well, let him stay there long enough,
he'll give you a bleeding ulcer.

12:58.461 --> 13:00.588
Judith said that too.

13:01.263 --> 13:02.389
Anyway, uh...

13:02.565 --> 13:04.692
..."Melatonin, a mouth guard-"

13:04.867 --> 13:09.167
I guess he grinds his teeth at night.
I myself have restless leg syndrome.

13:09.338 --> 13:12.068
But just the left leg,
right leg sleeps like a baby.

13:12.241 --> 13:13.299
What else, Herb?

13:13.742 --> 13:16.074
Well, I also got apnea
and I tend to drool a lot.

13:18.848 --> 13:21.339
- The list, Herb.
- Oh, right, yeah.

13:21.517 --> 13:22.609
Let's see, uh...

13:22.785 --> 13:24.252
..."A shower cap, a loofa mitt."

13:24.420 --> 13:26.945
And some sort of little stool
that elevates his feet...

13:27.122 --> 13:29.682
- ...while he's sitting on the toilet.
- What?

13:29.859 --> 13:32.191
Yeah, when the morning coffee
doesn't do the job...

13:32.361 --> 13:36.422
...having his feet up gives him that extra
leverage for a successful bowel movement.

13:37.166 --> 13:39.361
- You're kidding.
- No. Look.

13:39.535 --> 13:41.867
"For a successful BM."

13:42.304 --> 13:44.135
That would mean "bowel movement."

13:45.341 --> 13:48.242
Okay, fine.
Uh, guest bedroom's right down there.

13:48.410 --> 13:49.434
Oh.

13:49.612 --> 13:52.308
Hey, I just made a pitcher of margaritas.
You want one?

13:52.481 --> 13:56.713
Gee, I'll have to pass. Judith's waiting for me
to get back, and she gets really steamed-

13:56.886 --> 13:59.878
- Salt or no salt? You got it.
- Salt. Okay.

14:07.162 --> 14:09.494
This is so weird.

14:10.165 --> 14:13.623
It's just for a couple of days, Jake.
Don't make a federal case.

14:14.003 --> 14:15.994
This is probably gonna affect
my schoolwork.

14:16.171 --> 14:18.901
How? It's not like
your grades could get any lower.

14:19.074 --> 14:21.406
That's good, Alan.
Undermine his self-esteem.

14:21.577 --> 14:24.068
You see what I have to live with
on weekends?

14:24.246 --> 14:26.510
Nobody's talking to you.

14:28.851 --> 14:30.546
Where is he gonna sleep?

14:30.719 --> 14:32.482
I'm not a he, I'm your father.

14:32.922 --> 14:35.948
How'd you get to be my father
if you're not a he?

14:37.593 --> 14:38.924
We'll make up the couch.

14:40.262 --> 14:41.388
What about the guest room?

14:41.564 --> 14:44.124
That's not a guest room anymore,
it's Herb's train room.

14:44.300 --> 14:47.235
- His what?
- He's a model-train aficionado.

14:48.737 --> 14:51.934
- Aficionado?
- He works hard. He deserves a hobby.

14:52.374 --> 14:54.934
Sometimes he lets me wear the hat.

14:56.345 --> 14:59.337
I begged you for years
to let me turn that into a game room.

14:59.515 --> 15:02.313
- Bumper pool, Ping-Pong, something.
- Well, this is different.

15:02.484 --> 15:04.952
- How?
- Herb can play with his trains alone.

15:06.488 --> 15:08.752
I'm sure he does plenty of stuff
in there alone.

15:10.059 --> 15:12.152
- Excuse me?
- Nothing.

15:12.962 --> 15:14.020
I got it.

15:21.904 --> 15:24.134
This is so beautiful.

15:24.673 --> 15:25.697
Yup.

15:26.609 --> 15:28.133
Can I confess something, Charlie?

15:28.611 --> 15:29.635
What's that?

15:29.812 --> 15:32.872
I sometimes wonder about
the road not taken.

15:33.048 --> 15:34.379
Which road is that?

15:34.550 --> 15:36.541
Your road, Charlie.

15:36.719 --> 15:38.118
Oh.

15:38.287 --> 15:40.278
It's a good road, Herb.

15:40.456 --> 15:43.323
So it's not a matter of
"the grass always seems greener"?

15:43.492 --> 15:46.791
No, no. No, the grass
is pretty freaking green over here.

15:48.430 --> 15:49.954
Damn.

15:53.869 --> 15:55.496
Oops. That's me.

15:55.671 --> 15:56.899
I would hope so.

15:57.506 --> 15:59.599
It's the road taken.

16:00.609 --> 16:02.201
- You're not gonna answer it?
- No.

16:02.378 --> 16:07.281
- Judith will just harsh my mellow.
- Yeah. She's a mellow harsher.

16:07.449 --> 16:08.575
But I love her.

16:09.318 --> 16:10.683
That's nice.

16:10.853 --> 16:14.516
You know, in the boudoir,
we're very simpatico.

16:15.391 --> 16:16.790
Glad to hear it.

16:16.959 --> 16:18.517
On top of everything else...

16:18.694 --> 16:21.925
...she actually let me put my train set
in her back room.

16:45.954 --> 16:48.388
Damn cran-apple juice.

16:50.826 --> 16:53.124
I should start wearing a diaper.

17:43.912 --> 17:47.643
- It's about time you got home.
- Mmm.

17:49.918 --> 17:52.887
Is that an apology I'm feeling?

18:03.432 --> 18:04.421
Oopsie.

18:08.403 --> 18:11.065
- Where's my husband?
- Sleeping on the deck.

18:11.240 --> 18:13.970
- What? Why?
- He's drunk.

18:14.409 --> 18:15.637
Herb's not a drinker.

18:16.111 --> 18:17.942
No argument there.

18:18.113 --> 18:19.774
All right, here's how it's gonna go.

18:19.948 --> 18:23.714
I am taking him home with me,
and you are taking back your brother.

18:24.086 --> 18:25.917
How about this?

18:26.822 --> 18:30.485
You and Alan patch things up
and I keep Stretch out there.

18:30.659 --> 18:32.627
I've grown kind of fond of the big lug.

18:33.061 --> 18:34.892
Charlie, I'm in no mood.

18:35.330 --> 18:37.298
- That's not what I heard.
- What?

18:40.602 --> 18:42.797
I don't have time for this.
Alan, get in here!

18:42.971 --> 18:45.997
No.
- Do not make me come get you.

18:48.877 --> 18:52.176
Now, apologize to your brother.

18:54.149 --> 18:55.776
Do it.

18:59.288 --> 19:01.415
I'm sorry I made
such a big deal of everything.

19:01.590 --> 19:03.057
And?

19:04.393 --> 19:07.590
And you- You can keep the
24 dollars and 78 cents.

19:07.763 --> 19:11.028
- This was all about $24?
- Plus he tried to set me on fire.

19:11.200 --> 19:13.828
After he sucked my gas.

19:14.303 --> 19:16.965
Hey, baby.
When did you arrive on the scene?

19:17.639 --> 19:19.004
Just get in the car.

19:19.174 --> 19:21.039
Look, a poop stool.

19:21.777 --> 19:23.972
Um, I'm- I'm- I'm gonna need that.

19:27.249 --> 19:30.047
Well, you can pop a blood vessel
if you push too hard.

19:30.219 --> 19:31.709
Words to live by. Mm-hm.

19:31.887 --> 19:33.718
Herb, car.

19:33.889 --> 19:35.186
- Bye, Charlie.
- Bye, Herb.

19:35.357 --> 19:36.585
- Bye, Alan.
- Bye, Herb.

19:36.758 --> 19:40.194
- This was fun. Let's do it again.
- Now.

19:44.800 --> 19:45.892
Kind of like old times, huh?

19:47.502 --> 19:50.062
Judith kicking me out
and you taking me in?

19:52.641 --> 19:54.836
You are taking me in, aren't you?

19:55.544 --> 19:57.375
Give me one good reason why I should.

19:58.413 --> 20:02.247
Uh, well, we- We're-
We're family.

20:02.417 --> 20:04.578
Uh, brothers.

20:04.753 --> 20:08.189
We share blood and- And-
And history.

20:08.357 --> 20:10.882
We have a bond that unites us forever.

20:12.361 --> 20:13.919
No, what else you got?

20:15.297 --> 20:17.060
Okay, uh...

20:17.332 --> 20:19.232
...what about my French toast?
You like that.

20:19.668 --> 20:23.001
You know, uh,
thick and fluffy with cinnamon...

20:23.171 --> 20:25.036
...and powdered sugar?

20:25.574 --> 20:27.201
Mmm.

20:28.677 --> 20:30.577
- All right, you can stay.
- Really?

20:30.746 --> 20:32.179
No.

20:37.386 --> 20:39.513
Very funny. Ha, ha.

20:40.122 --> 20:41.555
Charlie?

20:46.695 --> 20:49.528
You changed the locks?

20:50.032 --> 20:52.364
I was only gone for six hours!

20:53.335 --> 20:54.768
Charlie?

21:00.342 --> 21:02.401
Oh, crap.

21:08.517 --> 21:11.247
Here you go. Black, two sugars.

21:11.420 --> 21:13.354
Double glazed.

21:13.522 --> 21:16.184
- Thank you.
- No, thank you.

21:16.959 --> 21:18.893
I can't believe Grandma fired me.

21:19.061 --> 21:21.928
Well, buddy, the labor market's
very competitive these days.

21:22.097 --> 21:25.555
There's always somebody
brighter and better willing to work for less.
